{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw","id":1109824,"title":"Looking for a flaw...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-30T10:32:54-07:00","id":1109824,"title":"Looking for a flaw...","content":"I know there's a four point Widderslainte flaw, but I've forgotten which book it's in. Could someone help, please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T10:53:47-07:00","id":1109836,"title":"","content":"I can't find any direct &quot;Widderslainte&quot; flaw anywhere - but there is one that pretty much is what it implies:<br /> <br /> M20 Book Of Secrets has &quot;Taint of Corruption&quot;, which is a 7(!) point flaw...which seems more fitting the gravity of the state, and being a Widderslainte is one of the options for it.<br /> <br /> If you are looking for a social flaw that handles being accused of being a Widderslainte..&quot;Probationary Member&quot; (4 point Flaw), or &quot;Notoriety&quot; (3 point flaw) would work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T12:38:13-07:00","id":1109867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1109836#post1109836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20 Book Of Secrets has &quot;Taint of Corruption&quot;, which is a 7(!) point flaw...which seems more fitting the gravity of the state, and being a Widderslainte is one of the options for it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> M20 Core book: &quot;Don't play as a nephandi, it will make you a terrible person.&quot;<br /> <br /> M20 Book of Secrets: &quot;Wanna be a widderslainte for 7 bonus points?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T15:09:16-07:00","id":1109942,"title":"","content":"Honestly, those flaws are rarely worth it for seven points, unless you intend to play a doomed, definitely bad end for your character. At least assuming the storyteller is doing their job. :-)<br /> <br /> ETA: if there is a Widderslainte flaw in one of the previous books, it'd probably be in Book of Shadows, Book of Mirrors, or one of the Books of Madness. I'd recommend checking there first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 06-30-2017, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T08:47:17-07:00","id":1110187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1109867#post1109867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> M20 Core book: &quot;Don't play as a nephandi, it will make you a terrible person.&quot;<br /> <br /> M20 Book of Secrets: &quot;Wanna be a widderslainte for 7 bonus points?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, the corebook advice refers to playing practicing Nephandi, whileas the flaw just gives you an aptitude for evil magic, which may be played in various different ways. After all, there is a definite difference between &quot;I rain down nasty magic on my enemies&quot; and &quot;I eat babies, rape innocents, and torture puppies to honor my dark master&quot;. The flaw does not seem much different in practice from that other flaw that gives you a lifebane aura (and they may even be different manifestations of the same curse). It all comes down on how you deal with it.<br /> <br /> Moreover, the flaw's writing at last gives official sanction to the notion that widderslainte status is potentially treatable, which is much welcome at my table. The idea that Nephandic taint is an irreversible condition across incarnations, and you are born doomed to choose being a walking, talking cancer to the Tellurian because of the wishes of your previous incarnation always rubbed me as terribly wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 07-01-2017, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T08:49:51-07:00","id":1110190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1109942#post1109942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, those flaws are rarely worth it for seven points, unless you intend to play a doomed, definitely bad end for your character. At least assuming the storyteller is doing their job. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>If the ST is playing this kind of Flaw as an inexorable doom no matter what the player and character do, then they are not doing their job well. There should always be a way or three potentially available to deal with the situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T09:14:20-07:00","id":1110218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1110190#post1110190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the ST is playing this kind of Flaw as an inexorable doom no matter what the player and character do, then they are not doing their job well. There should always be a way or three potentially available to deal with the situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? If that's the path the player and ST together want to take with the character, maybe there shouldn't be a way out. That may be the core of the story they want to have for this character. <br /> <br /> I remember playing a superhero Champions back in the day who the ST and I created to die and have that sort of thing happen. Why? Because that sort of thing happens in comics and it can happen and be some of the best story-telling ever (or it can be complete gratuitous crap), but the way Champions is typically set up, it's not going to happen to a normally built character. It worked. It was great. <br /> <br /> The analogy is a little rough around the edges but it's pertinent. Sometimes the crux of the game can be the player agreeing to place their trust in the hands of the ST and seeing what fun can be had dealing with the consequences. <br /> <br /> I've had a mage character in one of my games die horribly and suddenly the whole game changed over to being about saving his soul from the Hell it was locked in and bringing him back to life. No one telling them that it was (mostly) impossible for them to do so or that, if they were to try it, it would be HARD and there would be serious consequences had ANY effect. It was glorious. Even though their result was a bit cobbled together (e.g. they couldn't bring him back in his own body, so they had to find a body without a soul, and so on). <br /> <br /> In another game, the NPC who was the impetus to get the group together ended up being a 15 year old Widderslainte. Though the cabal didn't know it, her dark destiny was the reason for her kidnapping in the first session and the group gelled around rescuing her. When she finally turned bad, it was heartbreakingly tragic. Even she really didn't want to take that leap into the Abyss, she just couldn't help herself. A PC died trying to give her the choice he desperately wanted her to have and it changed nothing. Not that the group wasn't still trying to find a way to bring her back despite that until that game fizzled out. (I was doing about 4-6 hours of prep to every hour of gaming and just couldn't manage that any longer.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T10:16:14-07:00","id":1110243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1110218#post1110218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why? If that's the path the player and ST together want to take with the character, maybe there shouldn't be a way out. That may be the core of the story they want to have for this character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if a doomed character is the story the player wants to tell, then of course it is all right for the ST to go along with them. I was thinking of the case when the player picks this kind of flaw because they want to play the challenge of fighting against the curse and potentially succeeding, or using 'bad' powers to a good end, a la Spawn or Ghost Rider, and the ST instead feels entitled to pick it as an excuse to trap the character in an inescapable doom. I objected to Kalinara's statement because it made me think of hat kind of bad ST'ing. This kind of flaw should never mean certain doom unless player and ST agree the character is meant to be played that way. Simply putting the flaw on the character sheet means nothing because the player may easily mean to tell a different, less tragic kind of story.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T17:10:08-07:00","id":1110413,"title":"","content":"Some flaws are exactly what they say they are. I'll point out &quot;Dark Fate&quot; for example, which is a five point flaw, not a seven point flaw. And the rules are very clear about what that means. Why would a seven point flaw be any better?<br /> <br /> That's the cost inherent with taking flaws. You are giving the storyteller license to use those flaws to make things very difficult for your character. And in some cases, that's going to mean a bad ending. And a player accepts that when they take these (completely optional) flaws.<br /> <br /> Communication is important, of course. And if a player and storyteller agree that they want to do a story of a not completely screwed Widderslainte, that's one thing. But if someone is just taking this flaw because they want the points, or because it sounds like a cool story, then they should be prepared to play THAT story. And, at least if you're following the source materials, that's not going to be a happy one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 07-01-2017, 08:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T09:32:35-07:00","id":1110576,"title":"","content":"Nowhere in this Flaw's writeup it states picking it is tantamount to picking a death warrant for the character, on the contrary it indicates the curse its represents can be potentially removed. So there is implied no implied agreement in its purchase the story the player means to tell about it is one of inexorable doom. It is quite possible the intent behind it is to play Ghost Rider: the Mage or somesuch. There are several 5-7 dot Flaws in the M20 corebook and Book of Secrets and certainly not all of them are meant to mean the same character doom as Dark Fate, which is clearly and explictly marked as such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T11:41:05-07:00","id":1110606,"title":"","content":"I think it's funny that you seem to think a good storyteller is somehow bound to ignore ALL of the published material on Widderslainte, (with the possible exception of Amanda, who had an archmage's intervention preventing her reincarnation as a Widderslainte) to accommodate a player who wants to play a special snowflake AND get 7 freebie points out of the deal. (In contrast, Dark Fate only gives you 5. This is, in short, meant to be worse than that.)<br /> <br /> The flaw doesn't need to specify that the character is screwed because every book that addresses the subject has already said so.<br /> <br /> I would agree that a Widderslainte's story could be compelling, and if a player and storyteller mutually choose to change the setting enough to allow a happy ending, great. <br /> <br /> But you better make SURE you and your storyteller are on the same page, because there is nothing that requires a &quot;good&quot; storyteller to ignore all of the published material since 1993 just because a player unilaterally decides to take a 7 point flaw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 07-02-2017, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T06:31:54-07:00","id":1110816,"title":"","content":"First, the Flaw is meant to address various possible causes that create this kind of situation, read its writing, being Widderslainte is only one among several. Second, M20 comes last in the line and hence is more authoritative than everything pre-existing; it already made sizable changes to the setting (e.g. by making everything Avatar Storm-related strictly optional), so no surprise if it changes the status of the Widderslainte, too. Third, previous setting lore about the Widderslainte always made very little sense about the overall themes and metaphysics of Mage anyway, in pretty much no other case past lifetimes' experiences of the Avatar were supposed to have that kind of ironclad control on the thoughts, actions, and choices of the mage in their current life, it created myriad metaphysical plot holes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 07-03-2017, 10:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T07:07:30-07:00","id":1110831,"title":"","content":"I haven't read it, but wouldn't be the first time that a Merit/Flaw jumps the shark.<br /> <br /> Does it specify how can the Flaw be removed?...because if it doesn't I'm entirely free to say that it requires nothing less than Senex killing your character (as with Amanda)<br /> <br /> Does it say that &quot;being Widderslainte&quot; equals having this Flaw (that there's nothing more about being a Widderslainte than having this flaw), or rather that Widderslainte have the Flaw? (how it's this worded?) Because if it's like the latter, I can say that Widderslainte isn't doomed to be evil because they have the Taint of Corruption, but because they're Widderslainte","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-03-2017, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T07:14:15-07:00","id":1110834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">it already made sizable changes to the setting (e.g. by making everything Avatar Storm-related strictly optional)</div> </div> </div> </div>M20 has a Metaplot that assumes Avatar Storm happened.<br /> <br /> Stating in a sidebar that you can refuse to use it if you don't want to doesn't make the Storm any more optional than when I decided to ignore it back in Revised. It doesn't explain how to adapt the new metaplot to a world that never had the storm (it just says: well, everything it's still as it was in 2ed!)<br /> <br /> Seriously people: Do you really need a sidebar telling you: &quot;metaplot it's optional&quot; to feel entitled to ignore it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T09:42:48-07:00","id":1110895,"title":"","content":"Well, if you ask my opinion, it is previous setting lore that jumped the shark by implying Widderslainte status was irreversible and its carriers doomed to be evil, and this Flaw's writeup is merly attempting to jump back. If Nephandic corruption is so much more powerful and lasting across reincarnations than Awakened self-determination and whatever empowers Avatars and mages, and the Awakened can only deploy Gilgul as a destructive stopgap counter (maybe; the same setting lore implies perhaps soul-killing is not so effective or final as supposed), why haven't the Nephandi and their masters conquered the Tellurian and destroyed it or remolded it in their dark image long ago? The sect has been around for millennia and if one assumes lore about widderslainte is correct it should be steadily expanding its ranks every generation between what we are told is a significant number of newly-corrupted mages and all the reincarnating members that can only Awaken into ultimate evil, barring Gilgul. And it seems other mages aren't that effective or thorough in capturing Nephandi and sending them through the soul-killing ritual. This piece of setting lore seems nothing but yet another example of old WoD's unfortunate taste for angst for angst's sake tainting a game whose themes and playstyle were anything but doom-laden.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I reread the Flaw's wording. Broadly summarizing, it says being Widderslainte is one possible cause of having a Taint of Corruption but there are several possible others, such as demonic possession, the aftermath of a bad Quiet or Seeking, corrupt Resonance, deals with malignant Umbrood, a curse, a vile past life or wicked karma, Nephandic heritage, poor life choices, the influence of the Wyrm, ownership of tainted texts or artifacts, and so on. It tends to taint one's practices, instruments, spells, aura, dreams, and impulses towards corruption. In game terms it gives a bonus to wicked magick and a similar penalty to 'good' one. However it also explictly says it does not force or doom the character to do evil - one can resist its bad influence - and it is possible to defeat the curse, although it won't be an easy fight. An epic quest may allow to purge the taint (and buy off the Flaw) although it would be easier to go with the flow. Entities that may recognize such soul-stains tend to regard the character as a mortal enemy (e.g. werewolves), an object of pity and potential salvation (the nicer kind of mages), or possilby both.<br /> <br /> So having Taint of Corruption does not striclty equate being Widderslainte but the latter is one possible case for the Flaw's occurrence, and its writeup explictly says it does not force one to be evil - although it would be the easier course - and it may be potentially resisted and removed. Since this rule covers a more general case including various non-Nephandic possibilities, it does not say ToC is everything there is in M20 about being Widderslainte, but as far as it is concerned, such a status can be potentially resisted and overcome.<br /> <br /> As a matter of fact, if one reads ToC rules (and the ones for similar Psychic Vampire Flaw) together with the general ones for Resonance in the same book, these Flaws (and the Spark of Life Merit) seem notable cases of especially strong and entrenched resonances more than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 07-03-2017, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T09:57:44-07:00","id":1110902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1110834#post1110834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> M20 has a Metaplot that assumes Avatar Storm happened.<br /> <br /> Stating in a sidebar that you can refuse to use it if you don't want to doesn't make the Storm any more optional than when I decided to ignore it back in Revised. It doesn't explain how to adapt the new metaplot to a world that never had the storm (it just says: well, everything it's still as it was in 2ed!)<br /> <br /> Seriously people: Do you really need a sidebar telling you: &quot;metaplot it's optional&quot; to feel entitled to ignore it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course not, but M20 does a very nice thing to create a level playing field in the fandom between haters and fans of Revised stuff by explictly making all the most controversial Revised stuff optional. The pro-Revised faction can no longer claim to have an official seal of approval and the anti-Revised crowd no longer has to feel like second-class fans as canon goes. That M20 does not give much metaplot coverage to an updated version of the setting where things tended to stay the 2ed way means little, it may simply represent a limitation in available space, time, and effort of writing.<br /> <br /> Especially since M20 is a project truly and massively bursting at the seams about the material it strives to cover, up to the point it had to be split in a four-volume set thanks to a very successful kickstater, the last book (the 'bestiary' NPC one, but being told to contain some PC-relevant stuff too, such as a few especially outlandish Traits) is still being written, the M20 corebook set new records in the hobby for size, the Book of Secrets is as big as many vanilla corebooks, and M20 core, BoS, and HDYDT are packed tight with info.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 07-03-2017, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T18:43:28-07:00","id":1111094,"title":"","content":"I'm always willing to bend rules for the sake of awesomeness. ^^ We redeemed a BSD by mistake already. The rest of the PCs can choose to kill the Widderslainte pawn when they find out.... if they're willing to also kill the Marauder via psychic shock. They will, however, have to contend with the fae who don't like Dreamers being killed out of hand. Then things will get interesting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T09:22:31-07:00","id":1111299,"title":"","content":"I can't think of a time where I DIDN'T ignore the RAW to make a good story.... Redeem a Widderslainte? Why not?<br /> <br /> It's supposed to take hella-high Spheres to bring back the dead and/or not be possible and I let them go on a mystic treasure hunt and make deals with all sorts of questionable beings, and, when the shopping list was completed and the weird dance was done, the character was resurrected {sorta - it was his soul, but not in his original body, except for that tattoo they regrafted from his baby-momma who had grafted it onto herself, and so on...) without ANYONE having Life 5, Matter 5, Spirit 5 or whatever the requirements are or aren't right now. Which is a better game? The one where the ST says, &quot;You can't do that because the rules say so!&quot; or the one where the ST says, &quot;Well, it's never been done before to the best of your knowledge... You still want to try? Okay, what do you want to do next?&quot;<br /> <br /> After all, the PCs are the protagonists of your game, not the NPCs or the RAW. Like the characters in the movie or novel, they're supposed to be the ones who do the impossible thing no one else can do, unless that's not the game you're playing? I mean, sure, you can play a game where it's all doom and gloom and Kafka-esque fruitless striving. Again, why not? As long as that's the game that people want to play (or the character arc a player is looking to play), it's fine. And picking a Flaw with a high associated cost doesn't necessarily mean you are dealing with someone who wants the gloom and doom. It's important to put these things right out there on the table.<br /> <br /> I guess if the player is taking the Flaw purely for the points and never wants to pay the associated price (whether that's &quot;You are F*#$ED!&quot; or &quot;Man, no one knows a way around this.... Good luck finding it and there is a high chance of failure...&quot;) you have a problem, but it's more of a &quot;problem player&quot; problem than anything else.<br /> <br /> And, after all, the irredeemable Widderslainte is not a really a thing in Mage. Senex was able to deus ex machina around it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 07-05-2017, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T10:00:50-07:00","id":1111324,"title":"","content":"I agree 100% on that. I believe that Mage it's a game where <i>impossible</i> it's an expression used to remark just how EPIC it's what you're attempting.<br /> <br /> At the same time, and precisely because RAW isn't that important, I think it's unnecessary to point out to a Flaw's writting and say that, because the flaw suggests that something that has to do with being a Widderslainte can be healed, and don't turns you into a bad person, then it's clear that the writters have decided to take away all the doom and drama involved in having an inverted soul of previous editions.<br /> It seems like the kind of reasoning that a rules lawyer would do (Everything points otherwise, but there's this small paragraph in a new book that agrees with me, thus I'm right!). This is why I, being no layman about the rules, answered with an <b><i>objection!</i></b> of sorts.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-04-2017, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T11:59:30-07:00","id":1111374,"title":"","content":"Aleph's comment really hits the nail on the head for me.<br /> <br /> I'm definitely not opposed to the idea of player characters attempting, and succeeding, in an impossible quest. But that's why communication is really important. Personally, if I were running a &quot;redeem the Widderslainte&quot; plot, I'd probably try to discourage my players from choosing to play the Widderslainte themselves, for three reasons.<br /> <br /> The first is the frustration aspect. I'm honestly not sure what I'd require from players to actually succeed in this kind of quest, but there'd be a LOT of potential for failure. The player HAS to be on board with the idea that, more likely than not, their character will have a really painful ending, and that's a hard burden for a lot of players. It can be easier to accept failure when it's an NPC on the line.<br /> <br /> The second is that if we're talking about a group game as opposed to a one-on-one game, then there's a risk of one character monopolizing the entire story. That can be tricky to balance the focus. If the Widderslainte is an NPC, it's easier to keep the focus on the other players and their emotional reactions to events. The story then is less about whether or not they actually succeed and more about how the quest impacts each of them.<br /> <br /> The third is that having a player character as a Widderslainte pretty much ropes all of the other characters into this one, very specific story. It's very possible that the other players would have no interest in a redeem the Widderslainte quest. Or their characters, as created, would have no reason to want to undergo a quest like this. If the Widderslainte character is an NPC, then the players have more freedom to decide how they want to deal with the situation.<br /> <br /> But I think it's really important that a player who takes this flaw understands the World of Darkness doesn't require games to have a happy ending anyway. (There's a reason that Gehenna/Apocalypse/Ascension/Time of Judgment exist after all.) Choosing a flaw like this makes it even less likely. And the other players and storyteller are under no obligation to cater to one player's whims, unless it's a story that they ALL want to play.<br /> <br /> My original pithy comment was a bit too flippant I suppose, but the fact of the matter is that even if the players are on board with the idea of a cure the Widderslainte plot, we'd be talking realistically about a chronicle long plot that would involve a lot of pain, torment, and endless possibility for failure. Obviously, many players don't want to play a dark and tragic ending. But if that's the case, then they really should not be taking a flaw like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2430,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","user":"kalinara","date":". 07-04-2017, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T13:47:38-07:00","id":1111400,"title":"","content":"This is a crazy idea, but I think if someone wanted to play a Widderslainte that really tries to be &quot;good&quot;, or as good as possible, and yet respect the destiny of evil that should await the character...It may be neat to have a Degeneration system, like that of Vampire, Demon or even Wraith.<br /> <br /> Of course you can say that you are a Widderslainte, and act good nevertheless, but if you want to at least do a modicum attempt at respecting the themes of the Fallen, this would be cheating.<br /> <br /> A system of Degeneration can create the detachement from your character that you need in order to keep a will to be good, but still understand that you're becoming less and less good. It provides a measurement that takes a bit of the weight of interpretation out of your shoulders, and marks a line you can't cross if you don't want to be full &quot;unplayable&quot; Nephandi.<br /> Vampire plays very well with this, as vampires that try to keep their Humanity at higher levels soon discover that this it's easier said than done (as vampire world it's very violent). Humanity score works as a way to keep tabs on your degeneration in spite of the fact that you don't actively &quot;try&quot; to fall. You could even make it so that &quot;humanity&quot; cannot be recovered once lost (like Abominations) if you want the struggle to be especially harrowing.<br /> <br /> The Shadow in this case would be the Fallen Soul/Inverted Avatar, that pulls you into Nephandism. It would be like having a Nephandy trying to corrupt her, but this time the Nephandy it's her own soul that knows everything about her and can't be kept away. The Morality could be build arround ideals of Ascencion, thinking about how these can be twisted into Descencion.There will be a turning point in wich your character would become unapologetically evil, and turn into an NPC...Of course this isn't a desirable outcome, and thus searching for a way to heal your &quot;condition&quot; would be very desirable.<br /> <br /> What can the Inverted Avatar do to contribute to Descencion? Well, I'm not a fan of giving the Inverted Avatar more power than it should have...that being said there are several options dependant on the Avatar. that are well within the rules<br /> Of course a lvl 5 Manifest Avatar it's going to be much more dangerous than a lvl 1 Circunspect one. I would like my Widderslainte PC to be good sport and take a potent avatar, but shouldn't be mandatory unless it's painfully obvious that the player wants to cheat the curse.<br /> At the very least, I would say that even the weakests Avatars can make sure that their mages cannot ever succeed in a Search unless they loose a point of &quot;humanity&quot;, after all, it's the Avatar the one who judges (and yours it's an asshole). This, by itself, presents a strong moral chalenge that's not unlike what a character like Ghost Rider has to put trough-You want more power?, fine: are you ready to bargain with the Devil?.<br /> A really active evil Avatar may offer teaching (an Avatar can be your Mentor for Arete and Spheres), Past Lives, and more access to the Dream in exchange for a few bad acts.<br /> And all of this would be on top of the 7 lvl Flaw bonuses and penalties tempting you to the dark side. And that's before Banes, devils, and actual Nephandi take interest on you...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-04-2017, 04:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T15:37:16-07:00","id":1111427,"title":"","content":"Oh, I like that thought a lot. I think a modification of the Torment system could work really well in terms of incorporating ideas of synergy and resonance as well.<br /> <br /> It reminds me though that I have a vague recollection of one of the books mentioning gilgul as a possible, albeit painful, solution to the problem of a not-yet-fully-evil Widderslainte. I don't remember which book though, or whether the idea was explored in any depth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T16:20:57-07:00","id":1111445,"title":"","content":"IF that's the case, then hiding the Avatar in a Phylactery may be another solution. Less effective and much more risky, but with a lot of potential. Maybe a mage tried to isolate an Inverted Avatar to test cures, maybe she couldn't bear to kill the soul of a Nephandi that was her lover and thus decided to trap it for all eternity (which means, until the plot needs it :P)<br /> <br /> I can imagine a &quot;good&quot; Widderslainte having a malignant phylactery that she tries not to use to avoid it's influence, much like Elric of Melnibone would try to avoid using Stormbringer. But magick it's too useful...and if the character it's a PC, she will want to wield the POWER now and then <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T18:21:05-07:00","id":1111483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kalinara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1111427#post1111427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I like that thought a lot. I think a modification of the Torment system could work really well in terms of incorporating ideas of synergy and resonance as well.<br /> <br /> It reminds me though that I have a vague recollection of one of the books mentioning gilgul as a possible, albeit painful, solution to the problem of a not-yet-fully-evil Widderslainte. I don't remember which book though, or whether the idea was explored in any depth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or just fight going up in Arete. Since &quot;up&quot; is actually towards Decension....<br /> <br /> Or tie it into what used to be called paradigm but now doesn't have a name.... that set of ideas and practices that embrace the members of a Tradition and distinguish from others. For example, Senex was trying to de-Widderslainte Amanda via a very Chakravantri sort of Euthanatos route... purging her karma And so on through acts in accordance with dharma in a future incarnation. So, there might be something similar for others as well. Chorister Widderslainte might have to seek the intervention of the One (aka God) or its immediate subordinates (&quot;washed clean in the blood of the Lamb&quot;.... so where is that Holy Grail again?) And so on...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-04T22:55:05-07:00","id":1111562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1111483#post1111483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or tie it into what used to be called paradigm but now doesn't have a name.... that set of ideas and practices that embrace the members of a Tradition and distinguish from others. For example, Senex was trying to de-Widderslainte Amanda via a very Chakravantri sort of Euthanatos route... purging her karma And so on through acts in accordance with dharma in a future incarnation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder, do Euthanatoi go around doing the same for Technocrats, 'purging their karma' ? Cause according to considerations such as 'karma', the Order of Reason members and the Technocrats (especially the Syndicate) were and are definitely in need of it. More so than young Widderslaintes, I'd say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 07-05-2017, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T02:34:33-07:00","id":1111593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1111483#post1111483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or tie it into what used to be called paradigm but now doesn't have a name.... that set of ideas and practices that embrace the members of a Tradition and distinguish from others.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has a name..Focus. (Paradigm + Practice + Tools). Unless you mean the combination of Paradigm and Practice only, in which case..yeah. There is no name for that subset.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1111562#post1111562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder, do Euthanatoi go around doing the same for Technocrats, 'purging their karma' ? Cause according to considerations such as 'karma', the Order of Reason members and the Technocrats (especially the Syndicate) were and are definitely in need of it. More so than young Widderslaintes, I'd say.</div> </div> </div> </div>What they normally do is all about Karma. It's why the Chakravanti give people the Good Death in the first place - so they can take the whole reincarnation tour on the wheel again and try to be better in their next life.<br /> <br /> The difference between Widderslainte and, say, Technocrats is that the Euthanatos KNOW that a Widderslainte will fall to the same evil over and over, no matter how many times they die..hence Senex having needed to go another route. And yeah, it's very vague in regards to what he exactly DID. Ajax' explanation makes sense, but I don't think there is any official description of what Senex did to Amanda. Or rather, her previous incarnation Mercedes.<br /> <br /> Though the Wiki mentions, now that I check it, that Senex 'Killed Mercedes, and Magically altered her Avatar so she would not be reborn Widderslainte'. So maybe it wasn't that different from normal Chackravanti proceedings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-05-2017, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T07:00:40-07:00","id":1111640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1111593#post1111593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference between Widderslainte and, say, Technocrats is that the Euthanatos KNOW that a Widderslainte will fall to the same evil over and over, no matter how many times they die.</div> </div> </div> </div>How and from where do they know this?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T08:24:35-07:00","id":1111666,"title":"","content":"That's an interesting question: The fact that Widderslainte's Avatar reincarnates Inverted it's against Euthanatos Paradigm...nobody should be forever denied of the chance to purify the soul...however, Euthanatos do know this fact as per their Book (of course, they refuse to believe that this it's impossible to solve).<br /> <br /> But how do they know this?<br /> <br /> Seeing an Avatar it's possible, M20 has the rules. Magick can interact with Avatars. That being said, searching for an avatar that has been reincarnated it's possible (and not only for Senex :P ). Eutanatos have a whole &quot;house&quot; (don't remember the name, but it's in the revised book) that dedicates itself to follow souls trough their reincarnation cycles, and they're supposed to have extensive information on the history of avatars...they're perhaps the greatest experts on Avatar reincarnation.<br /> <br /> Having this in mind, it's not too hard to believe that Euthanatos have discovered Inverted Avatars through various incarnations, and, contrary to the mages expectation, they're always corrupted...This is how, I think, Euthanatos know that Widderslainte are &quot;different&quot;. Other Avatars &quot;cleanse&quot; themselves trough death (or so Euthanatos believe), not the inverted ones (not that an Euthanatos it's going to admit this, surely Inverted avatars just need more time...or something)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-05-2017, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T09:38:29-07:00","id":1111684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1111593#post1111593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It has a name..Focus. (Paradigm + Practice + Tools). Unless you mean the combination of Paradigm and Practice only, in which case..yeah. There is no name for that subset.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Focus is PERSONAL. Each mage has one. It's made up of three parts. One of which is largely irrelevant to most issues concerning actual effects (Paradigm) and the other two are critical. Focus is a good thing, a thing that was never defined this well (or in this way) before, but it is NOT and never has been what &quot;paradigm&quot; used to mean. <br /> <br /> That thing I was talking about that made one Sect different from another. One Chorister can have a completely different Focus than another in all three parts (and in each of the sub-parts of the Instruments) and everything about those parts can be described in a very different way (say.... a jazz soloist with a set of very Secular Humanist style Universalist underpinings to a completely visceral faith vs. a tone deaf Orthodox rebi with a vast knowledge of Judaic law and the Kabbalah with incisive logical understanding worthy of Sherlock Holmes). And yet... they are both members of the same Sect. SOMETHING ties them together. And it's not a mandated Specialty Sphere, since every group now has a few to choose from. It's not a common Practice that all Choristers use, at least in part, because there is a list of options that is explicitly wide open. It's that missing something that was meant with one of the common (though, admittedly, especially in hide sight, imprecise) meanings of &quot;paradigm&quot; before M20. <br /> <br /> That has no name now and no formal place in the rules. But either it's still there and just being ignored in favor of Focus, or, really, there ARE no such things as Sects anymore. Just a vast sea of Orphans with membership cards to organizations of arguably less than immediate relevance or importance. As in, much less important than the Orders in Awakening or the Fellowships in DA..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T09:50:00-07:00","id":1111689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1111562#post1111562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder, do Euthanatoi go around doing the same for Technocrats, 'purging their karma' ? Cause according to considerations such as 'karma', the Order of Reason members and the Technocrats (especially the Syndicate) were and are definitely in need of it. More so than young Widderslaintes, I'd say.</div> </div> </div> </div>Karma is accumulated when dharma is ignored. It's not &quot;doing bad stuff&quot; (though it can be) Maybe the Syndicate members are precisely and completely following their dharmas? In which case, killing them is the Chakravanti failing at their dharma and it is the Chakravanti, not the Syndicate member, who is accumulating karma. Time for a Rinse-Cycle-Repeat on their Avatar.<br /> <br /> Parashurama, an incarnation of Vishnu, got pissed off at the entire kshatriya varna for doing warlike things. Which is their dharma. He killed off all the male kshatriya. He was the one who accumulated karma not the kshatriya who were just doing their jobs no matter what Parashurama thought about what they were doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 07-06-2017, 08:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T11:39:15-07:00","id":1111745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That thing I was talking about that made one Sect different from another. One Chorister can have a completely different Focus than another in all three parts (and in each of the sub-parts of the Instruments) and everything about those parts can be described in a very different way (say.... a jazz soloist with a set of very Secular Humanist style Universalist underpinings to a completely visceral faith vs. a tone deaf Orthodox rebi with a vast knowledge of Judaic law and the Kabbalah with incisive logical understanding worthy of Sherlock Holmes). And yet... they are both members of the same Sect. SOMETHING ties them together. And it's not a mandated Specialty Sphere, since every group now has a few to choose from. It's not a common Practice that all Choristers use, at least in part, because there is a list of options that is explicitly wide open. It's that missing something that was meant with one of the common (though, admittedly, especially in hide sight, imprecise) meanings of &quot;paradigm&quot; before M20.<br /> <br /> That has no name now and no formal place in the rules. But either it's still there and just being ignored in favor of Focus, or, really, there ARE no such things as Sects anymore. Just a vast sea of Orphans with membership cards to organizations of arguably less than immediate relevance or importance. As in, much less important than the Orders in Awakening or the Fellowships in DA..</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, sometimes, it may actually be a political decision strictly based on a wrong stereotype. Case of most Dreamspeakers, a bunch of dudes that deal with Umbrood that haven't more in common with each other than with the angel summoners of the OoH. A lot of them only accept to &quot;belong&quot; to their &quot;tradition&quot; when the Technocracy it's on their doorstep (Albeit even the Dreamspeakers have specific camps that have, at least, unified goals, if not belief).<br /> <br /> Other times, this &quot;paradigm&quot; implies a method or ideal that it's held by every member of the Tradition, which transcends its differences. Case of the Choristers, all of them believe that Faith it's what matters to do magick. Faith in what it's debatable to the point that an atheist with strong hopes for humanity qualifies (albeit it woud be very fringe), but faith it's important (to the point that it's even suggested to change True Magick for True Faith in their book, as a very extreme choice)<br /> <br /> There are Traditions more unified on common principles and <i>Focuses</i> than others. For a Hermetic, it's almost granted that your brother/sister will have a Focus compatible enough to cast rituals together, if your pal it's from another House (especially from Ex-Miscelanea) it may be necessary to make a traduction between the focuses, but <i>normaly </i>it will be easier than to work with another Tradition. For a Dreamspeaker this is far from granted, the sacred pipe of one may have very little to add to the high rituals of the other, if a Dreamspeaker can work in concert with another it has little to do to their belonging to the same Tradition.<br /> <br /> So, I would say that, sometimes, this &quot;paradigms&quot; are very real, to the point that they can manifest in rules like being able to &quot;share&quot; Artifacts or the beneffits of a Realm's Reality Zone, cast rituals together without fuss, and share magical knowledge. Other times are just there to unify a bunch of very different Crafts under the same flag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T14:22:13-07:00","id":1111807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1111593#post1111593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though the Wiki mentions, now that I check it, that Senex 'Killed Mercedes, and Magically altered her Avatar so she would not be reborn Widderslainte'. So maybe it wasn't that different from normal Chackravanti proceedings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've always figured that there were a lot of factors that went into Senex's work that may (or may not) be unique to the situation. Obviously, a big part is that Senex himself is an archmage. But it always seemed significant to me that, per the splat fiction, Mercedes herself hesitated and allowed him to act. It wouldn't have been enough to save her if there wasn't an impossibly powerful archmage at hand, but since there was, it basically became her Darth Vader in Return of the Jedi moment. <br /> <br /> It's likely pretty much unrepeatable, because you'd need an archmage with Senex's expertise and a Nephandi who, in that split second, would actually allow it to happen. The latter may be harder to achieve than the former.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T19:25:00-07:00","id":1111944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1111745#post1111745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, sometimes, it may actually be a political decision strictly based on a wrong stereotype. Case of most Dreamspeakers, a bunch of dudes that deal with Umbrood that haven't more in common with each other than with the angel summoners of the OoH. A lot of them only accept to &quot;belong&quot; to their &quot;tradition&quot; when the Technocracy it's on their doorstep (Albeit even the Dreamspeakers have specific camps that have, at least, unified goals, if not belief).<br /> <br /> Other times, this &quot;paradigm&quot; implies a method or ideal that it's held by every member of the Tradition, which transcends its differences. Case of the Choristers, all of them believe that Faith it's what matters to do magick. Faith in what it's debatable to the point that an atheist with strong hopes for humanity qualifies (albeit it woud be very fringe), but faith it's important (to the point that it's even suggested to change True Magick for True Faith in their book, as a very extreme choice)<br /> <br /> There are Traditions more unified on common principles and <i>Focuses</i> than others. For a Hermetic, it's almost granted that your brother/sister will have a Focus compatible enough to cast rituals together, if your pal it's from another House (especially from Ex-Miscelanea) it may be necessary to make a traduction between the focuses, but <i>normaly </i>it will be easier than to work with another Tradition. For a Dreamspeaker this is far from granted, the sacred pipe of one may have very little to add to the high rituals of the other, if a Dreamspeaker can work in concert with another it has little to do to their belonging to the same Tradition.<br /> <br /> So, I would say that, sometimes, this &quot;paradigms&quot; are very real, to the point that they can manifest in rules like being able to &quot;share&quot; Artifacts or the beneffits of a Realm's Reality Zone, cast rituals together without fuss, and share magical knowledge. Other times are just there to unify a bunch of very different Crafts under the same flag.</div> </div> </div> </div>That the Big Three (Choristers, Hermetics &amp; Verbena) creating several of the other Traditions by &quot;othering groups together&quot; is absolutely a historical reality. But, then again, so was Bonisagus gathering together a random assortment of wizards doing very different things and making the Order of Hermes. After a few hundred years, those groups had gelled enough to have a collective identity that distinguishes them from other groups. By this point in time, those groups the Hermetics later ended up forcing together have probably created something based on their commonalities. &quot;Dreamspeakers&quot; is not just an agglutinated mass of what Baldric La Salle, Valoran and Nightshade thought of as &quot;foreign savage mages&quot;, it's something more than it's constituent parts (and, essentially, was that from the very start, considering the attitude of its founders, Naioba and Star-of-Eagles). The Euthanatos is a little more difficult because there isn't really anything in common between the groups as basic as animistic tendencies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T22:41:28-07:00","id":1111984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1111944#post1111944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That the Big Three (Choristers, Hermetics &amp; Verbena) creating several of the other Traditions by &quot;othering groups together&quot; is absolutely a historical reality. But, then again, so was Bonisagus gathering together a random assortment of wizards doing very different things and making the Order of Hermes. After a few hundred years, those groups had gelled enough to have a collective identity that distinguishes them from other groups. By this point in time, those groups the Hermetics later ended up forcing together have probably created something based on their commonalities..</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes...but identity or broad mindset is not magickal Paradigm. As the books themselves show in the Chorister example characters, a Voudun Witch might as well fit into the Choristers as she fits into the Verbena.<br /> And, here is the important part: A particular Voudun Witch from the Choristers might actually have the very same Faith-driven paradigm as a particular Voudun Witch that belongs to the Verbena. Heck, it might be literally the same paradigm. Imagine two sisters growing up, getting taught by the same traditional (non-capital t) mentor, but one ultimately ending up in the Choristers, the other in the Verbena, simply for political reasons.<br /> <br /> You are RIGHT, of course, that each Tradition tends to have the most people of a certain nature or set of Paradigms (plural here) - that's where their stereotypes come from - but no Tradition is made of a single Paradigm. not even under Revised rules. Paradigm always was a (shareable to a degree) personal thing, and people with like-minded Paradigms usually gathered in a Tradition's sub-groups for that very reason, and the broad edges of the Traditions were always blurry in regards to one another. At least between some of them.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy's Conventions are more uniform of course, with way less variety of Paradigms inside the single Conventions, but that's because each of them is driven by each Convention's partylines that do not value individuality of belief, but conformity.<br /> <br /> The only Tradition that comes closer to this than the others is the Order of Hermes, and as you mentioned even the OoH had to invent more and more Houses in order to handle the different Paradigms in its midst. Heck, House Ex Misc is essentially the catch-all. But what ties the OoH together is history (even pre-council history), rules, their structure, ranks and initiations, and their mindset of becoming masters over the forces of Magick. But that - again - is not Paradigm.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But either it's still there and just being ignored in favor of Focus, or, really, there ARE no such things as Sects anymore. Just a vast sea of Orphans with membership cards to organizations of arguably less than immediate relevance or importance. As in, much less important than the Orders in Awakening or the Fellowships in DA.. </div> </div> </div>&lt;annd my phone client nom'd the edit of myreply to this..&gt;<br /> <br /> Well, the definition of Orphan in the mind of the Traditions is..anybody not belonging to the Traditions. A Witch that leaves the Verbena because some Leadership or other annoys her, or because she got tossed out because of misdeeds and then joins no other tradition is an Orphan. But her Paradigm about how Magick works has remained the same. Heck, the Hollow Ones, despite being an organized group, were pretty much labeled 'Orphans' by the Traditions. Naturally all Mages that are purely self-taught and never were in a Tradition fall under the same label.<br /> <br /> Ultimately this whole Argument pretty much boils down to semantics, and Paradigm's ambiguity - being able to mean a Mage's very specific belief, a set of beliefs, or the broad strokes that the Traditoons represent (Machines, Faith, Spirits etc.)<br /> In my mind Paradigm always was the very specific belief of an individual Mage, so the 'paradigm' part in M20's 'Focus' fits how I read it to a T. Your mileage may vary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-06-2017, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-05T23:44:35-07:00","id":1111993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1111689#post1111689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Karma is accumulated when dharma is ignored. It's not &quot;doing bad stuff&quot; (though it can be) Maybe the Syndicate members are precisely and completely following their dharmas? In which cse, killing them is the Chakravanti failing at their dharma and it is the Chakravanti, not the Syndicate member, who is accumulating karma. Time for a Rinse-Cycle-Repeat on their Avatar.<br /> <br /> Parashurama, an incarnation of Vishnu, got pissed off at the entire kshatriya varna for doing warlike things. Which is their dharma. He killed off all the male kshatriya. He was the one who accumulated karma not the kshatriya who were just doing their jobs no matter what Parashurama thought about what they were doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>And why would Widderslaintes accumulate karma due to ignoring dharma, according to the ideas of the Chakravanti?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1111666#post1111666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's an interesting question: The fact that Widderslainte's Avatar reincarnates Inverted it's against Euthanatos Paradigm...<br /> Having this in mind, it's not too hard to believe that Euthanatos have discovered Inverted Avatars through various incarnations, and, contrary to the mages expectation, they're always corrupted...This is how, I think, Euthanatos know that Widderslainte are &quot;different&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there anywhere a definition of what actually the Chakravanti (or other Traditions members) mean when they say that Widderslainte Avatars are 'corrupted'? What is the specific, practical problem(s) with the Widderslaintes and their Avatars?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T01:14:54-07:00","id":1112005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1111993#post1111993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there anywhere a definition of what actually the Chakravanti (or other Traditions members) mean when they say that Widderslainte Avatars are 'corrupted'? What is the specific, practical problem(s) with the Widderslaintes and their Avatars?</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes a Nephandus is *not* the fact that they are evil, or do bad things. Somebody like that is just a bad person who also, coincidentally, happens to be a Mage.<br /> A Mage who eats babies for breakfast might be an insane psychopath, or somebody worshipping demons, but they are not necessarily a Nephandus. Metaphysically their Avatar is still normal, and still strives for Ascension and enlightenment of that Mage.<br /> <br /> They can be redeemed, they can potentially be turned towards a different path. They are simply a potential a**hole of a human, that also does Magick in their spare time.<br /> <br /> <br /> The step to actually becoming a doomed Nephandus, the single thing that actually connects them all, is the fact that they voluntarily (and/or delusionally) stepped through the Cauls - essentially the analog process to the Black Spiral Dancers walking the Spiral - and they emerge with their Avatars inverted.<br /> That's the common (and defining) thing about Nephandi - their Avatars are twisted and 'inverted', and said Avatar's driving goal becomes Descension, not Ascension. And they will always drive the Mage towards the same, no matter the incarnation.<br /> <br /> And now we come to Widderslainte. Widderslainte are *born* with inverted avatars. That's what defines them. They are doomed from birth. Nephandi from the get-go.<br /> That's why, no matter how many times they are killed, that inverted Avatar will reincarnate and strive for the same ultimate descent.<br /> <br /> <br /> The big Irony of the war against the Nephandi is, that killing a Nephandus without Gilguling them first essentially causes a new Widderslainte to be born somewhere down the line...<br /> <br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-06-2017, 05:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T02:59:17-07:00","id":1112021,"title":"","content":"Oh, and a little late, but while we are on the topic of Widderslainte..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1109867#post1109867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M20 Core book: &quot;Don't play as a nephandi, it will make you a terrible person.&quot;<br /> <br /> M20 Book of Secrets: &quot;Wanna be a widderslainte for 7 bonus points?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>..yeees and no. To a person wanting to actually full-on play a corrupting, evil Nephandus and having fun doing so, this would be a *Merit*.<br /> <br /> Actually, it's quite a nasty relevation: There are Nephandi out there that get -2 to their base difficulty to wreck shit.<br /> A Nephandus with that (to them) Merit gets a base difficulty of 6 to tossing fireballs down the middle of Broadway. With some Quintessence, that goes down to difficulty 3. *In front of Sleeper witnesses*. Insert jaw-drop sound here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T04:20:20-07:00","id":1112038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div cla