elevation: There are Nephandi out there that get -2 to their base difficulty to wreck shit.<br /> A Nephandus with that (to them) Merit gets a base difficulty of 6 to tossing fireballs down the middle of Broadway. With some Quintessence, that goes down to difficulty 3. *In front of Sleeper witnesses*. Insert jaw-drop sound here.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's already been hinted that Nephandi aren't affected by the Avatar Storm as much as regular mages, and Book of Madness Rev directly states that the Qlippothic Spheres are capable of feats that the regular spheres are just unable to do without support from other spheres, such as Qlippothic Prime able to drain an unwilling person of their quintessence, yes all of it. Or Qlippothic Matter able to, not just transmute, but obliterate, as in transform it into the very antithesis of its own being, bring something to nothing.<br /> <br /> Who's to say their corrupting bonuses don't extend to disbelief and paradox as well?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T04:39:02-07:00","id":1112043,"title":"","content":"In 1rst Edition Book of Madness Qlippothic Entropy at level 5 was able to &quot;turn something into nothing&quot;, causing the greatest damages of all magick back then. Successes x 5<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's already been hinted that Nephandi aren't affected by the Avatar Storm as much as regular mages</div> </div> </div> </div>They are affected, though, as they had to invent a few Rotes to bypass it in Infinite Tapestry...However, in the Book of Worlds it has been stated (and I think it was never refuted) that Marauders and Nephandi are immune to Disembodiment.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T05:53:09-07:00","id":1112066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1111984#post1111984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes...but identity or broad mindset is not magickal Paradigm. As the books themselves show in the Chorister example characters, a Voudun Witch might as well fit into the Choristers as she fits into the Verbena.<br /> And, here is the important part: A particular Voudun Witch from the Choristers might actually have the very same Faith-driven paradigm as a particular Voudun Witch that belongs to the Verbena. Heck, it might be literally the same paradigm. Imagine two sisters growing up, getting taught by the same traditional (non-capital t) mentor, but one ultimately ending up in the Choristers, the other in the Verbena, simply for political reasons.<br /> <br /> You are RIGHT, of course, that each Tradition tends to have the most people of a certain nature or set of Paradigms (plural here) - that's where their stereotypes come from - but no Tradition is made of a single Paradigm. not even under Revised rules. Paradigm always was a (shareable to a degree) personal thing, and people with like-minded Paradigms usually gathered in a Tradition's sub-groups for that very reason, and the broad edges of the Traditions were always blurry in regards to one another. At least between some of them.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy's Conventions are more uniform of course, with way less variety of Paradigms inside the single Conventions, but that's because each of them is driven by each Convention's partylines that do not value individuality of belief, but conformity.<br /> <br /> The only Tradition that comes closer to this than the others is the Order of Hermes, and as you mentioned even the OoH had to invent more and more Houses in order to handle the different Paradigms in its midst. Heck, House Ex Misc is essentially the catch-all. But what ties the OoH together is history (even pre-council history), rules, their structure, ranks and initiations, and their mindset of becoming masters over the forces of Magick. But that - again - is not Paradigm.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &lt;annd my phone client nom'd the edit of myreply to this..&gt;<br /> <br /> Well, the definition of Orphan in the mind of the Traditions is..anybody not belonging to the Traditions. A Witch that leaves the Verbena because some Leadership or other annoys her, or because she got tossed out because of misdeeds and then joins no other tradition is an Orphan. But her Paradigm about how Magick works has remained the same. Heck, the Hollow Ones, despite being an organized group, were pretty much labeled 'Orphans' by the Traditions. Naturally all Mages that are purely self-taught and never were in a Tradition fall under the same label.<br /> <br /> Ultimately this whole Argument pretty much boils down to semantics, and Paradigm's ambiguity - being able to mean a Mage's very specific belief, a set of beliefs, or the broad strokes that the Traditoons represent (Machines, Faith, Spirits etc.)<br /> In my mind Paradigm always was the very specific belief of an individual Mage, so the 'paradigm' part in M20's 'Focus' fits how I read it to a T. Your mileage may vary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, the old idea of a group paradigm that identifies a Sect is pretty much gone. It's all just Orphans carrying membership cards in groups that really don't have an intrinsic value past the fact that they are relics from old editions of the game because they have some political (not magical) value. <br /> <br /> A Voudoun Witch (which is something that in parsing, should make one's head throb with dire agony) would never have been a Chorister before, would never fit into the previous iterations of the Chorus pre-M20 and is pretty much a special snowflake situation, much like a Widderslainte who is not one in any meaningful sense since they aren't going to Descend, etc. In fact it's worse, because, without some serious convolutions, there aren't many coherent stories that make that character make sense at all. Previously, if a Chorister found that Orphan/newly Awakened (because, with the finders-keepers/pile-on default implicit in the game, almost all characters start as just-Awakened Orphans who get scooped up and schooled into a &quot;real&quot; Tradition) would have given basic instruction in how not to get yourself killed doing magic then passed them along to a see where they fit better, probably starting with the Verbena. <br /> <br /> Personal paradigm is &quot;shareable&quot; up to a point. When it gets to the point that the character has a personal paradigm that has pretty much nothing in common with the vast majority of the members of the Sect, they aren't really a member of that Sect in a meaningful magical sense and something of a fly in the ointment in a sectarian/social sense. The Chorus is eccumenical up to a point, but there is a fundamental, if diffuse, orthodoxy. Because there has to be. Humans don't form groups that have no group identity, no shared baseline. Each Sect has a culture and culture is inherently othering. Meaning there are some people who don't belong and, if they don't have options to go out and find a group they do fit with (Yay! Thanks for having all those different groups Tradition-high-ups!), they get relegated to a marginalized role in the group they are forced to stay with. There is SOMETHING that makes Choristers Choristers and not Hermetics, and it's not just that Valoran was one of the original dudes, e.g. the difference between Choristers and Dreamspeakers is not just an accident of history. It's not even hard to figure out what that is. It's that magic is faith and that faith is in a monotheistic or monolatrist or hinotheistic for some values of hinotheistic universe. There is SOMETHING that makes Choristers different from Dreamspeakers, even though both of them have a version of &quot;faith is magic&quot;, in that they have faith in different thing - the above vs . faith in an animistic universe, irrespective of the relative hierarchy or power of the spiritual entities in play. <br /> <br /> That Witch isn't an Orphan in the sense of the Orphans who are self-trained mages whose paradigms are purely personal and who have collectivized because the group ID they can gel around is &quot;we are all the same in that we are all different from everyone else&quot;. Which, if not for the stance of all the other Sects, would be a very tenuous identity indeed and wouldn't hold together. That Witch is an ex-pat Verbena. She's at best a &quot;political&quot; Orphan. She can be &quot;redeemed&quot; and come back if she is willing to take her licks for leaving or the poltical/social situation back in Verbena-land changes and she doesn't feel excluded anymore, etc. She's going to be an outsider among the Orphans because, no matter how you slice it, she doesn't really get where they are coming from. Their mindsets are fundamentally different. It's not even that, over time, she can become a &quot;magical&quot; Orphan without having to relearn/rebuy her Spheres from the ground up. If she does so, she will be hewing to the core of the Orphans and will become &quot;one of them&quot; and will have othered herself out of the Verbena beyond her history.<br /> <br /> The Union doesn't have this problem to any great degree as it's Sects are purpose built and the system was devised to handle this sort of situation, even when it does breakdown a little. The Union WILL find a box for you, even if the fit isn't perfect to start with. It will be. <br /> <br /> It's not semantics and it's not a &quot;thing&quot; personal to me. It's a huge gaping missing piece from the game in its previous iterations and M20. And it's not even unintentional. Brucato has outright said that his idealized perception of the game is essentially all Orphans. And he wrote that in. Which meant he wrote other things out. And the game's new default is all these individuals that, realistically, wouldn't have a prayer of hanging together in groups beyond the size of a cabal. (Note the example of a cabal with which we are provided in the Quickstart) It would be &quot;it's us against the world&quot; until it wasn't survival on the line and the group would drift or, more likely tear itself apart. It's worse than a music band as these people don't even have that one thing, music, in common. It can be a setting for Mage that you like, but, like bending things another way, it will and does cause its own problems... namely that Traditions aren't really an actual thing that makes a lot of sense and the Union just doesn't at all anymore, because there really can't be conformity in the viewpoint you've adopted. <br /> <br /> And, bending it back to the topic at hand, it means that there can't be an argument about some kind of &quot;absolute&quot; Widderslainte under the new &quot;Paradigm&quot; chosen for this iteration of the game, because each Widderslainte is their very own special kind of mage and there are no other mages like them. (Just like every Chorister is their very own Chorister and doesn't have to have a thing in common with any of the others, and, in fact, doesn't and shouldn't) And that's even though we sitll have the baggage of a Nephandi is a Nephandi is a Nephandi. And we see that tension in the RAW now. In one place the Nephandi are irreparably damned and a redeemed Widderslainte story is &quot;doing in the impossible&quot;, while, over here, we have a Flaw that presents Widderslainte as a lifestyle choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T05:57:53-07:00","id":1112068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1111993#post1111993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And why would Widderslaintes accumulate karma due to ignoring dharma, according to the ideas of the Chakravanti?<br /> <br /> <br /> Is there anywhere a definition of what actually the Chakravanti (or other Traditions members) mean when they say that Widderslainte Avatars are 'corrupted'? What is the specific, practical problem(s) with the Widderslaintes and their Avatars?</div> </div> </div> </div>They might not. But they probably would, as they probabaly don't have a dharma as there is no acceptable role in the universe that being a Nephandi would fulfill. That's probably why they are target number 1. They aren't criminals being criminals, and, in doing so, providing a stepping stone from what is below criminal-hood to what is above it, they are nihilistic anarchist terrorists that want to tear down the whole system. Maybe the system is fine with their being a role in the system that is anti-system, but most systems don't work that way, or they don't stay working for very long that way.<br /> <br /> The other part was already answered 110%","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T06:15:05-07:00","id":1112074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1112068#post1112068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They might not. But they probably would, as they probabaly don't have a dharma as there is no acceptable role in the universe that being a Nephandi would fulfill.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming this point of view - how do the Chakravanti know this in regards to the Nephandi, as compared to thinking that the Technocrats are fine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T07:00:49-07:00","id":1112087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1112066#post1112066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Voudoun Witch (which is something that in parsing, should make one's head throb with dire agony) would never have been a Chorister before, would never fit into the previous iterations of the Chorus pre-M20 and is pretty much a special snowflake situation</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, it might have been 'Voodoo Priestess. I was paraphrasing from memory and wanted to use the more proper Voudun, and made it Witch. My bad!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1112066#post1112066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not semantics and it's not a &quot;thing&quot; personal to me. It's a huge gaping missing piece from the game in its previous iterations and M20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which begs the question why I understood it as I described - before M20 even was released. Revised era.<br /> Or, to put it differently, I didn't notice any change in the very concept of the Traditions at all when reading M20. Maybe *my* interpretation was always off-kilter and just so happens to perfectly match thew new M20 wordings of it all.<br /> I wonder what other folks in the thread think.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T07:15:05-07:00","id":1112089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are RIGHT, of course, that each Tradition tends to have the most people of a certain nature or set of Paradigms (plural here) - that's where their stereotypes come from - but no Tradition is made of a single Paradigm. not even under Revised rules. Paradigm always was a (shareable to a degree) personal thing, and people with like-minded Paradigms usually gathered in a Tradition's sub-groups for that very reason, and the broad edges of the Traditions were always blurry in regards to one another. At least between some of them.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Which begs the question why I understood it as I described - before M20 even was released. Revised era.<br /> Or, to put it differently, I didn't notice any change in the very concept of the Traditions at all when reading M20. Maybe *my* interpretation was always off-kilter and just so happens to perfectly match thew new M20 wordings of it all.<br /> I wonder what other folks in the thread think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're right as to the way things are and have been for long. There was fringe examples like yours in Revised Trad books- However, I think the loose joints that make the stereotypes and like-mindedness of each Tradition and sub-tradition can be conceptualized to some extent, thus allowing to discriminate from fringe Paradigms that are in the Tradition because reasons that have little to do with belief, and those that share the common beliefs or meta-paradigm of the group. Surely it's easier to form a comunal Reality Zone with people that are like-minded than otherwise. <hr /><br /> Probably the most solid rule ever to sepparate one Traditon from another (in a somewhat, but not entirely, artificial way) was from 1rst Edition. In that old and flawed edition there was a rule to teach Spheres to another mage (it involved a roll, and paying less xp for the Sphere level). The difficulty was higher if the teacher didn't belong to the same Tradition of the student. It was also implied that this teaching between mages of different Traditions wouldn't even be possible without the theoretical &quot;frame&quot; of the Sphere System, as understood in game (a common languaje to speak about magick). Of course, in 1rst Edition Paradigm was <i>undeniably </i>window dressing for the Purple Paradigm, so it doesn't count<br /> <br /> I think that, while 1rst Edition rule feels artificial and doesn't jive with modern editions, it has it's charm to think that Traditions invented certain common &quot;languages&quot; and &quot;concepts&quot; that teach to all their members and allow to have easier comunication between their members individual Paradigms. This way you can also justify the &quot;bonuses&quot; of the Traditions, like having less difficulty with multiple perceptions when you are a Cultist, or having a Totem if you're a Dreamspeaker, as &quot;secrets&quot; that are teached within the Tradition (of course, this ended in M20. In Revised you needed to be Dreamspeaker or have a Merit to have a Totem. Not any more).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-06-2017, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T07:31:57-07:00","id":1112094,"title":"","content":"Conceptually, I think that NO mage's Paradigm it's entirely individual. Mentors and other external influences shape the Paradigm, connecting the mage with other Paradigms and to the Consensus as a whole.<br /> <br /> In fact, the concpet of Paradigm originaly meant the general school of tought that your Mage defended. I.E: &quot;my paradigm it's witchcraft&quot;, naturaly you haven't invented witchcraft, you learned about it from somewhere, and you would likely want join and learn with other witches. Joining the Chorus...it's a bit odd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T08:44:20-07:00","id":1112126,"title":"","content":"On my way home I was pondering this discussion some more, and I think I boiled it it down to an essential question that shows the two different viewpoints that seem to be happening.<br /> <br /> We'll take the Choristers again, since they are our prime example in this discussion:<br /> Faith. Faith is the thing that defines the Chorus as a group. It's their shtick, their garb, the keyword that, as a group, separates them as a prime identity trait from 'Witchcraft' Verbena, 'Personal Dominion and Structured Rules' Hermetics, 'Shamanism' Dreamspeakers, etc. etc.<br /> That is fine and we are in agreement. Now, taking the Choristers again, is 'Faith', the word and concept that is associated with them the most...<br /> <br /> <br /> A) ...the common paradigm of the Celestial Chorus.<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> B) ...the thing that all the paradigms in the Celestial Chorus have in common.<br /> <br /> <br /> To me it always has been 'B', and the basis and line on which the different paradigms in that Tradition manage to communicate and get along with. It's the guidelines under which the many different groups got put together as 'Traditions' in the first place, back after ye olde dark ages.<br /> <br /> So far my viewpoint. What I wonder is, if you answer 'A'...what is your word for what's called 'Paradigm' in answer 'B'?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 07-06-2017, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T10:06:46-07:00","id":1112173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the thing that all the paradigms in the Celestial Chorus have in common. </div> </div> </div>That was all that Plato needed to create his theory of Forms/Ideas , though! :P <hr /><br /> My answer would be that because B), therefore A).<br /> <br /> The thing that all the paradigms in the Celestial Chorus have in common <b>it's </b>the common paradigm of the Celestial Chorus.<br /> <br /> Of course, this breaks down very quickly when we sart to dig fringe characters and divergent sub-sects, that are as old as the first Tradition Book (but who knows, maybe the<i> Ideal Chorister</i> exists somewhere in the Astral Umbra <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> It's my understanding that, in Mage, Paradigm was always used in various ways:<br /> <br /> &quot;What's <i>your </i>Paradigm?: <i>M</i>y character believes in this and that&quot;<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> &quot;Hermetics believe in this and that, for someone with an Hermetic Paradigm...&quot;.<br /> <br /> You can even get up a level and speak of the &quot;Technocratic Paradigm&quot; . All are correct. One can distinguish one from the other by the use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-06-2017, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T10:23:21-07:00","id":1112183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1112173#post1112173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's my understanding that, in Mage, Paradigm was always used in various ways:<br /> <br /> &quot;What's <i>your </i>Paradigm?: <i>M</i>y character believes in this and that&quot;<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> &quot;Hermetics believe in this and that, for someone with an Hermetic Paradigm...&quot;.<br /> <br /> You can even get up a level and speak of the &quot;Technocratic Paradigm&quot; . All are correct. One can distinguish one from the other by the use.</div> </div> </div> </div>And *that* is why I wrote earlier<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ultimately this whole Argument pretty much boils down to semantics, and Paradigm's ambiguity - being able to mean a Mage's very specific belief, a set of beliefs, or the broad strokes that the Traditions represent (Machines, Faith, Spirits etc.)<br /> In my mind Paradigm always was the very specific belief of an individual Mage, so the 'paradigm' part in M20's 'Focus' fits how I read it to a T. Your mileage may vary. </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I might not be as nuts as I was starting to think, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T17:27:17-07:00","id":1112423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1112074#post1112074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assuming this point of view - how do the Chakravanti know this in regards to the Nephandi, as compared to thinking that the Technocrats are fine?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there are varnas that have those kinda of dharmas.... The Syndicate is fulfilling the dharma of the Vaishya merchant caste. N.W.O. and the Progenitors are both certainly in line with the dharma of the Brahmin. Iteration-X as well, as scientists and engineers might fit there, or, depending, maybe as Sudra workmen. VEs are a little more difficult, though post Avatar Storm, counter Threat Null are definitely Kshatriya and that's without plumbing the depths of subcastes, regional and chronological variations.<br /> <br /> But the point is, almost everything the Technocracy does has an accepted role in the baseline society from which the Chakravanti draw their beliefs. And the varnas are still a very real thing and can profoundly affect selection of modern vocations. (Except when they don't.)<br /> <br /> However, the Nephandi don't have an acceptable role. They are the opposite of following a dharma.<br /> <br /> Plus, if you look at their souls, they're icky.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 07-06-2017, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T17:33:14-07:00","id":1112428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1112173#post1112173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was all that Plato needed to create his theory of Forms/Ideas , though! :P <hr /><br /> My answer would be that because B), therefore A).<br /> <br /> The thing that all the paradigms in the Celestial Chorus have in common <b>it's </b>the common paradigm of the Celestial Chorus.<br /> <br /> Of course, this breaks down very quickly when we sart to dig fringe characters and divergent sub-sects, that are as old as the first Tradition Book (but who knows, maybe the<i> Ideal Chorister</i> exists somewhere in the Astral Umbra <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> It's my understanding that, in Mage, Paradigm was always used in various ways:<br /> <br /> &quot;What's <i>your </i>Paradigm?: <i>M</i>y character believes in this and that&quot;<br /> <br /> and<br /> <br /> &quot;Hermetics believe in this and that, for someone with an Hermetic Paradigm...&quot;.<br /> <br /> You can even get up a level and speak of the &quot;Technocratic Paradigm&quot; . All are correct. One can distinguish one from the other by the use.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gave this a like because of it's value for it's inherent truth. (Especially the Platonic part.)<br /> <br /> However, it does represent very sloppy terminology in a game. Like the meanings of &quot;level&quot; in D&amp;D back in the day (your character's level, the level of the dungeon, the level of the spell being cast, etc.) And it's even worse for a game in which the on-the-table rules by which we play the game also exist pretty much exactly the same conceptually inside the game universe as well. (It's a problem for the players and ST and for the characters equally and respectively.) And it's even worse when its over what is a defining aspect of the game. In fact, in some ways, it is the &quot;coolness factor&quot; of Mage. And it's a big, sloppy, hot mess of slippery verbiage.<br /> <br /> .And, away from the post to hand....<br /> <br /> That means, pretty much, that if one is okay with it, that's fine, but that doesn't make it okay universally. (Otherwise it wouldn't come up explicitly so much and implicitly so very many times more.) The fact that some people have a personal take on it because they needed to go out and come to terms with it on a level of individualized understanding is actually part of the problem. As is the fact that the situation was deliberately made more difficult and that was labeled as a feature and not a bug. Which is not true, except if the game is handled in a way that doesn't make much sense with the associated world-building.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 07-06-2017, 08:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T23:16:12-07:00","id":1112521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1112423#post1112423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, the Nephandi don't have an acceptable role. They are the opposite of following a dharma.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would the Chakravanti (or other Tradition members) consider the Nephandi 'the opposite' of following a dharma/dharmas?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1112423#post1112423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Plus, if you look at their souls, they're icky.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where exactly is this written?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T05:09:35-07:00","id":1112605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1112521#post1112521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would the Chakravanti (or other Tradition members) consider the Nephandi 'the opposite' of following a dharma/dharmas?<br /> <br /> Where exactly is this written?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The job of the Euthanatos is to safeguard the Cycle of Existence, the dharma of the universe.<br /> <br /> The avocation of the Nephandi is to derail the Cycle of Existence and undo the dharma of the universe, starting by accumulating and encouraging the accumulation of as much karma as possible and moving on from there.<br /> <br /> There is no varna with that dharma. That's un-dharma. There really isn't a conceptual framework for it beyond karma, but it is actually so much more. If the purpose of existence is too move souls through the cycle of reincarnation, hopefully to higher and higher dharmas, but, if not, there is a system in place to encourage that movement and to regulate it if it's not in the &quot;wrong&quot; direction. Nephandi are that wrong direction. They aren't people getting rewarded with promotions or demoted for lack of competence (with the lure of future reward if they demonstrate competence in their new, lower position), they are terrorists, not just subverting the system, but bringing it crashing down into ruin. &quot;Destroying all jobs and tearing down the factory&quot; is not a valid job description.<br /> <br /> As to how to suss them out. There is the problem of edition with that. So, &quot;it depends&quot; is one answer. Usually it's something to do with Resonance, though the meaning of that changes. So, using all the appropriate Spheres for detecting that (whatever those might happen to be, usually something to do with Mind and/or Prime). Not foolproof. Karma is going to show up pretty much the same in Nephandi vs. non-Nephandi and various forms of Quiet are going to look like/are karma. So offing everyone in Quiet might make things easy. (Though, if expiation of karma during a lifetime is a thing, then maybe not.)<br /> <br /> If Qlipothic Spheres are a thing, then looking for the consequence of the use of those Spheres. (An Alternate Sphere system now usually doesn't mean just getting a two-in-one deal, so nuts to that, I say, but that's just what I say.) Of course, conjunctional effects with Prime and/or Entropy can pretty much do everything a Qlipothic Sphere is said to do (and often said to be the only way to do, but, nuts to that too, because there are always many ways to accomplish anything in Mage). That might be fairly easy to detect with just 1 dot in the Sphere in question, particularly a Pattern Sphere.<br /> <br /> Just using the right Spheres in the right way, might catch them. Time might be a great way to do it. Look down the timeline and weigh the deeds. With conjunctional Mind, weight the intent as well. With Time and Spirit follow the soul into the next incarnation. Or use Mind. Some thoughts are Nephandi thoughts, though the thinker may not be one, they could be...<br /> <br /> Sp, no easy way. If there were, Nephandi would get caught to the point of extinction. So use a few of the above. Get a friend or two that can use different detection methods and compare notes. And you still might be wrong. Especially since, when what you are doing is using a variety of hammers to hit a very particular kind of nail and a lot of other things also look like nails.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 07-12-2017, 09:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T03:04:41-07:00","id":1114997,"title":"","content":"Our resident pawn is an NWO Blacksuit, who's psionic in Life and Mind. They also have Demented Eidolon. There isn't much to go on about Widderslainte Technocrats, though they needs twice as much Quintessence and gains far too much Paradox. So far, they Awakened after setting their intended target and bodyguards on fire by thinking about it, burnt out the minds of the Psych Ops agents trying ( and botching ) the attempt to Socially Condition them, killed the Operator responsible, and all but killed a dozen people in two days. With limited sensory affects -- and the Marauder around --, no one's noticed the Qlippothic Spheres. They've been put in the &quot;punishment unit&quot; with the rest of the Reality Deviants, who they consider to be family, with no memory of anything before Processing.<br /> <br /> Will a pack of Unseelie fae notice Nephandic corruption? Or would they consider it to be an extremely Unseelie Dreamer?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T03:56:45-07:00","id":1115012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saint Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1114997#post1114997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They also have Demented Eidolon.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the &quot;Demented Eidolon&quot; ?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T11:07:57-07:00","id":1115144,"title":"","content":"Something masquerading as their (nonexistent, Reality Deviant) wife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","user":"Saint Michael","date":". 07-12-2017, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T05:09:42-07:00","id":1115477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saint Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1109824-looking-for-a-flaw?p=1114997#post1114997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Will a pack of Unseelie fae notice Nephandic corruption? Or would they consider it to be an extremely Unseelie Dreamer?</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be that they notice something, but if they place it in the right ballpark?<br /> <br /> They can most certainly sense that it is not good, but the \u201cfaction\u201c is not a simple matter of resonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T09:06:38-07:00","id":1115550,"title":"","content":"Thankfully, no one's Ailil. So they can't auto detect the widderslainte. They didn't notice the BSD's corruption either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}